& [SourceIntegrity] passed at 12065 bytes SHA256 4D873CFAB7146193E015183C92095FE14BC86011797968CD4DD3AEFF582FE958
& [Baseline] is pushed commit 1c841bf0972057a115e54feed26f34925f92da57
& [FormationAuthority] exists because reader binding observation and normalization semantics are documentary
& [ImplementationAuthority] is absent because I03A I03B and I03C are inactive and jsonschema is absent from the workspace lock

& [Correction1] qualifies schema acceptance
  + an observation is acceptance by exact jsonschema version feature draft format and numeric representation profile
  + it is not proof of universal mathematical Draft 2020-12 interpretation
  + source bytes and I03B number tokens remain evidence whenever Value projection changes spelling or precision class

& [Correction2] closes numeric projection classes
  + integer token exactly representable as i64 is exact_i64
  + nonnegative integer outside i64 but within u64 is exact_u64
  + finite fraction or exponent accepted by serde_json is finite_f64 and explicitly approximate as a mathematical decimal representation
  + integer outside u64 or any nonfinite or parser-unrepresentable token is representation_exhausted
  + representation_exhausted never becomes schema rejection or agreement

& [Correction3] makes format behavior explicit
  + call should_validate_formats false and should_ignore_unknown_formats true
  + register no custom formats
  + int64 uint32 and uint64 remain annotations and typed deserialization supplies representation enforcement
  + reliance on version-dependent default format behavior is forbidden

& [Correction4] corrects no-retriever wording
  + jsonschema ValidationOptions always owns a retriever interface and defaults to DefaultRetriever
  + under default-features false its HTTP and file branches fail closed but the interface still exists
  + future I03A activation must supply an owned zero-sized CantorDenyRetriever whose every retrieve call returns a deterministic denial without I/O
  + fragment-only reference preflight remains primary and any deny-retriever invocation becomes internal_fault
  + no caller-provided registry retriever or resource callback is accepted

& [Correction5] corrects meta-schema independence
  + draft202012 meta validation is recorded before validator construction
  + jsonschema 0.49.2 public ValidationOptions build also performs schema validation and does not expose without_schema_validation
  + construction therefore repeats an internal schema gate and may not be called operationally independent from meta validation
  + separate observations mean separately reported outcomes rather than disjoint library execution

& [Correction6] binds current serde dependencies without freezing future activation prematurely
  + current lock contains serde 1.0.229 checksum 4148590afebada386688f18773da617792bf2ef03ffc1e4cbd2b1d45b023e0ba
  + current lock contains serde_json 1.0.151 checksum c841b55ecdae098c80dcae9cf767f6f8a0c2cdb3416bbef72181df4d0fe73f14
  + jsonschema is absent
  + I03D activation must bind the exact post-I03A lock because dependency resolution may change serde-family versions

& [Correction7] closes the response-root relation
  + base response schema is 53014 bytes SHA256 40FD8536021892ADB35CECBCA717AD2CA68FA5125A3C027FC8274364FCE1B77C
  + preparation response schema is 53021 bytes SHA256 9D51B85036B9A4FF7C519693F60C6ECF99C7CC5E529EF7DB423365D776C7B51A
  + their schema values are exactly equal after removal of root dollar id
  + root identity intended use document digest and fixture policy remain distinct and cannot be merged by equal validation behavior

& [Correction8] separates reader refusal phases
  + schema rejected requires completed validator iteration with one or more normalized rule findings
  + schema Value parse failure or numeric representation exhaustion occurs before validation and cannot count as rejected
  + typed data error is typed rejection while typed syntax or EOF after faithful ingress is internal parser disagreement

& [Correction9] closes finding overflow atomicity
  + collect at most 256 normalized findings plus one checked overflow observation
  + encountering a 257th produces exhausted stage normalization with observed minimum 257
  + bounded prefix may be retained only as non-authoritative diagnostic evidence and cannot accompany accepted or rejected disposition

& [Correction10] closes stable schema rule scope from exact artifact audit
  + current instance finding families are additional_properties any_of constant enum maximum minimum maximum_length minimum_length one_of pattern required type and unique_items
  + dollar ref failures belong to preflight or internal fault
  + format is annotation only
  + unseen error kinds cause profile_drift rather than dynamically expanding the stable enum

& [Correction11] closes serde locator meaning
  + category line and column under the exact activated serde_json version are identity-bearing reader evidence
  + they are not JSON Pointer paths or source-byte offsets
  + no inferred field path is claimed without a separately activated path-aware dependency or owned mechanism

& [Correction12] closes output intended-use responsibility
  + typed serialization proves only that ProcedureToolResponse serialized
  + root-specific intended use is an admitted fixture assertion and later corpus obligation
  + I03D preserves that assertion but does not semantically validate it

& [Correction13] closes future source touch
